course: dictionary
lesson: 13994
title: Loquacious and other grand words for talking
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Loquacious is a grand, formal word. It means talking a lot, or being very chatty. A loquacious person never seems to run out of things to say.
explain: «My little brother is loquacious at breakfast, telling us every detail of his dream.» The clues are telling and every detail: he says a lot, so loquacious must mean chatty. Check by swapping in chatty: "he is chatty at breakfast" still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: You will meet loquacious in exams, older books and as a joke. Everyday words that mean nearly the same are chatty and talkative. Loquacious sounds more formal and grand, so pick it when you write carefully.
fact: Loquacious means talking a lot; very chatty.
fact: Loquacious is an adjective. It changes to more loquacious and most loquacious.
fact: «She was loquacious all through the car journey.» means she talked a lot the whole way.
fact: Chatty and talkative are everyday words with nearly the same meaning as loquacious.
fact: Loquacious is a formal word, so you will see it more in writing than in everyday speech.
exercise: «Our neighbour is so loquacious that she talks to the postman for half an hour.» What does loquacious mean? | *Very chatty | Angry and loud | Lost and confused | Very quiet and shy
exercise: Which everyday word means about the same as loquacious? | *Chatty | Hungry | Tidy | Quiet
exercise: «Grandma was loquacious at the party, telling everyone about her trip.» Which words are the best clue to its meaning? | Grandma and the party | She was tidy | Her trip was long | *Telling everyone about her trip
test: «The loquacious parrot chattered all morning, and nobody got a word in.» What does loquacious mean in this sentence? | *Talking a lot | Silent | Sleepy | Colourful
test: My cousin never stops talking, so she is the ___ person in our family. Which word fits? | Quietest | *Most loquacious | Loquacity | Loquacious
exam: «At the school concert, Priya was so loquacious that the teacher had to ask her to let others speak.» What is the best meaning of loquacious? | *Talking a lot | Very quiet | Very tired | Very kind
